Z||000000||Ralph||09-13-2000||07:31 PM||||Everyone......<BR>Today I was on the phone with a local auto parts company to order an alternator. When he told me the price I exclaimed I only want an inexpensive alternator cause I intend to sell the car. His remark was "don't sell that Fiero" I asked why? His reply, He supposedly has inside information that GM dealers, especially Pontiac, have been advised by the factory to accept any and all Fieros for trade in and the factory will issue a check for each one taken in and take them away. Away where? The guy at the parts store is also a Fiero owner.  I can't tell you any more than this. Could this be a rumor? How about you folks? Can anyone add any information to this? Have I been taken in?  Comments will be appreciated.<BR> <BR>  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/yellowformula/LittleFiero.jpg"> <BR>  <B>  Ralph </B>||||reg||1
